    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d826680_8893d005",
        "filename": "common/usb_common.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 735,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-02T05:28:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would anything weird/bad happen if both the TCPC and the PP detected and reacted to the FRS signal?",
      "parentUuid": "7e8f9c0d_69de44a0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 735,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 735,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "21d5560552c48d048e543e77e5a5db03f3eef139",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f87f49a0_f651aed4",
        "filename": "common/usb_common.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 735,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-02T16:38:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "trembyle uses the NCT3807 TCPC and AOZ1380 PPC.  In this configuration the TCPC has handles a lot of the FRS but I have a board level function that sets the AOZ GPIO signals to support this. If the CONFIG_USB_PD_FRS_xxx defines manage this condition path then it should not affect anyone that does not have this configuration.",
      "parentUuid": "4d826680_8893d005",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 735,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 735,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "21d5560552c48d048e543e77e5a5db03f3eef139",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8baa17bb_93a7a0b0",
        "filename": "common/usb_common.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 735,
      "author": {
        "id": 1347775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T19:37:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We definitely can\u0027t have both the TCPC and PPC detect FRS, then we would make multiple calls to the PE when we see an FRS.\n\nThe situation I\u0027m worried about is when we have both a TCPC and a PPC which support the FRS trigger. This is not an issue on Zork since the PPC doesn\u0027t have an FRS trigger. But I understand now why Denis is asking for this since the PPC may need configured even if it doesn\u0027t have an FRS trigger.\n\nI think within the PPC driver, maybe we can have conditional paths to handle this issue. For the SYV682, enabling FRS could mean gpio setting and register setting, but to what values depends on where the trigger is. If it is in the TCPC, we need to explicitly disable the CC FRS trigger in the PPC.\n\nI do think we still need the 2 config flags though, I don\u0027t know any other way to handle it in the very real PS8815+SYV682 situation (right now the PS8815 driver doesn\u0027t support FRS so it isn\u0027t a real issue yet, but it could in the future).\n\nFor this function, can we just always call both of these? They would get stopped if the FRS enable function is not defined in the PPC. I think Denis was alluding to this in the last patchset.",
      "parentUuid": "f87f49a0_f651aed4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 735,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 735,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "21d5560552c48d048e543e77e5a5db03f3eef139",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c690b9e9_c1bfb03e",
        "filename": "common/usb_common.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 735,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-04T14:39:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not suggesting two different means of detecting FRS. Trembyle requires both the TCPC and PPC to be enabled/disabled in order for the signals to detect properly.  Our PPC does not have any smarts in it and just requires some GPIO manipulation.",
      "parentUuid": "8baa17bb_93a7a0b0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 735,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 735,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "21d5560552c48d048e543e77e5a5db03f3eef139",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
